<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Reset (230)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>reset
reset &lt;zone&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>reset udgaard
</pre>
<p>Resets a zone at once, instead of waiting for its next reset: the zone's 
reset commands are carried out, loading the monsters and things that are 
missing, up to the numbers its builder set. Without a name, it 
resets the zone you are in. Nothing that is already there is removed: to 
clear a room first, use <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Purge</a>.
</p><p>It is logged.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Purge</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Load</a>
</pre>




</div>